{"schema":"mcpgit.table-batch-transaction.v1","transaction_id":"7da4e206-d05b-5d87-bcd4-d7bcce7c68c0","idempotency_key":"7da4e206-d05b-5d87-bcd4-d7bcce7c68c0","actor":{"kind":"github-action","repository":"yxsicd/agentlabrelease","runId":"36381431940"},"recorded_at_unix_ms":1790573677159,"tables":[{"path":"program_facts","operations":[{"op":"insert","operation_id":"4ce6d02f-e4e1-575b-a5c0-09198c9d4fe7","key":"agent-analysis-backup-extension-ability-entry","row":{"id":"agent-analysis-backup-extension-ability-entry","kind":"analysis","payload":{"agentProposal":{"automaticPromotion":false,"schema":"agentlab.maintainer_skill_fact_proposal.v1","sourceAssessmentSha256":"dea08fd641817141df7fe909d25c8d6c42d333173e12a63a8f56db4e8bac04f1"},"dimensions":["behavior","boundary","relations","responsibility"],"evidence":[{"gitBlobOid":"2cedb74107adfc8929705f014c9018961c0aacf6","path":"OtaBackup/entry/src/main/ets/entrybackupability/EntryBackupAbility.ets"},{"gitBlobOid":"53024e8f020cc0824592631ba6924108c8028f0f","path":"OtaBackup/entry/src/main/module.json5"},{"gitBlobOid":"78f40ae7c494d71e2482278f359ec790ca73471a","path":"OtaBackup/entry/src/main/resources/base/profile/backup_config.json"},{"gitBlobOid":"091797f50409f128c08442915b02ae52d3df6299","path":"OtaBackup/entry/src/main/ets/entryability/EntryAbility.ets"},{"gitBlobOid":"8e2d24ad42693fc877d51bb7820f0a9da68fa135","path":"OtaBackup/entry/src/main/ets/pages/Index.ets"},{"gitBlobOid":"1898d94f58d6128ab712be2c68acc7c98e9ab9ce","path":"OtaBackup/entry/src/main/resources/base/profile/main_pages.json"}],"id":"agent-analysis-backup-extension-ability-entry","interpretation":"EntryBackupAbility.ets is the module's declared backup/restore seam: it extends @kit.CoreFileKit BackupExtensionAbility with log-only onBackup/onRestore stubs; onRestore branches on bundleVersion.name starting '0.0.0.0' (comment-marked HarmonyOS-to-NEXT migration) versus other scenarios. It is reachable only via declarative wiring: module.json5 registers it as type 'backup' with srcEntry pointing at this file, exported:false, and metadata ohos.extension.backup referencing $profile:backup_config, whose allowToBackupRestore:true opts the module into backup restore. The UI side is independent: EntryAbility (mainElement) loads 'pages/Index' per main_pages.json; Index is a RelativeContainer whose @State message toggles 'Hello World' to 'Welcome' on click. Maintenance contract: keep srcEntry strings, $profile resource names, and exported class names synchronized; honor onRestore's documented synchronous-await contract for async work; keep the placeholder hypium suites under src/test and src/ohosTest resolvable; oh-package dependencies are empty, so @kit.* imports must resolve from the SDK; release obfuscation stays disabled though obfuscation-rules.txt holds -enable rules.","kind":"analysis","limitations":["Whether the OS backup framework ever invokes onBackup/onRestore for this module, and whether allowToBackupRestore:true actually enables system backup, is unproved: the SDK framework contract was not executed or observed, only the declared registration was read.","Buildability is unproved: hvigor and the @ohos/hvigor-ohos-plugin hapTasks pipeline were never run, so the claim that hapTasks plus the @kit.* imports compile into a HAP for targets 'default' and 'ohosTest' remains an inference from configuration text.","The meaning of the '0.0.0.0' bundleVersion.name prefix as a HarmonyOS-to-NEXT migration marker is asserted only by in-file comments; it was not verified against CoreFileKit BundleVersion documentation.","The effect of the empty mock-config.json5 object and of the -enable-* rules in obfuscation-rules.txt while release obfuscation has enable:false is inferred, not demonstrated."],"repositoryId":"guide-snippets","scopeSkillIds":["skill-scope-guide-snippets-otabackup-entry"],"sourceRevision":"71bbb3916625c8d9a370b7a1989b3a7f82090525"},"payloadSha256":"ea243190eba92e2348786bfb462f5f52d957783666c6a4f347b94a4e92757073","repositoryId":"guide-snippets","sourceRevision":"71bbb3916625c8d9a370b7a1989b3a7f82090525"}},{"op":"insert","operation_id":"c710c49c-0ced-5606-8ea3-038d1e7a052b","key":"agent-analysis-distributed-ability-connection-collab-entry","row":{"id":"agent-analysis-distributed-ability-connection-collab-entry","kind":"analysis","payload":{"agentProposal":{"automaticPromotion":false,"schema":"agentlab.maintainer_skill_fact_proposal.v1","sourceAssessmentSha256":"2c08a3a3dcfc68218003c3e0bb79fd5813bfe9dae7c48d8ae3f297da072e17bc"},"dimensions":["behavior","boundary","relations","responsibility"],"evidence":[{"gitBlobOid":"a6bc7a4c2076ef1e30c87ed814e7d8f7c3c22b7e","path":"DistributedCollab/entry/src/main/ets/pages/Index.ets"},{"gitBlobOid":"988a093b0a45c6f6f7877606050ef888ae72735c","path":"DistributedCollab/entry/src/main/ets/entryability/EntryAbility.ets"},{"gitBlobOid":"67273aa6e30514237ea5f8e720023057d0af3de6","path":"DistributedCollab/entry/src/main/module.json5"},{"gitBlobOid":"49291ea87bc9a94bb57858f8a317b498e960cba0","path":"DistributedCollab/build-profile.json5"},{"gitBlobOid":"10cda399b0aec3099b257299a57d284393e4e55a","path":"DistributedCollab/entry/oh-package.json5"}],"id":"agent-analysis-distributed-ability-connection-collab-entry","interpretation":"Buildable 'entry' module of the DistributedCollab sample: page Index.ets plus UIAbility EntryAbility.ets showing cross-device collaboration via the abilityConnectionManager API. Responsibility: keep manifest, page registry, resources, stub Hypium tests, and both sources coherent. Entry chain: module.json5 mainElement EntryAbility loads 'pages/Index' (main_pages.json) via onWindowStageCreate; parent build-profile.json5 binds module 'entry' at ./entry, so manifest, page profile, and parent module table must stay aligned. Relations flow via AppStorage: EntryAbility writes sessionId/isConnected/receiveMessage from connection callbacks; Index reads them with @StorageLink. Both files duplicate on(connect/disconnect/receiveMessage/receiveData) registration and UTF-8 TextDecoder decoding, so callback changes must be mirrored. Behavior is button-driven: createAbilityConnectionSession -> connect -> sendMessage/sendData -> destroyAbilityConnectionSession, plus inbound onCollaborate accepting via collabToken. Cautions: Index requests CAMERA/MICROPHONE/media permissions absent from module.json5, and bundleNames differ ('com.example.remotephotodemo' vs PeerInfo 'com.example.myapplication').","kind":"analysis","limitations":["Unproved that distributedDeviceManager.createDeviceManager('com.example.remotephotodemo') succeeds at runtime: it is a system API gated by permissions and no execution was observed; only the try/catch with hilog logging is evidenced in Index.ets.","Unproved that the AppStorage key 'pixelMap' bound by @StorageLink in Index.ets is ever written: no producer of that key exists anywhere inside the scope, so the binding may be dead or fed from outside the boundary.","Unproved whether the PeerInfo bundleName 'com.example.myapplication' matches the actually installed peer HAP; the sample's own device-manager bundleName differs and no packaging config in scope confirms either name.","Unproved that the module builds or that the Hypium suites (Ability.test.ets, LocalUnit.test.ets) pass: they are stub assertContain cases and no build or test run was performed."],"repositoryId":"guide-snippets","scopeSkillIds":["skill-scope-guide-snippets-distributedcollab-entry"],"sourceRevision":"71bbb3916625c8d9a370b7a1989b3a7f82090525"},"payloadSha256":"3e0fa4ff0dd11030e117f8f6b156766e72e017dbc6811f134466716d5228f44b","repositoryId":"guide-snippets","sourceRevision":"71bbb3916625c8d9a370b7a1989b3a7f82090525"}}],"results":[{"operation_id":"4ce6d02f-e4e1-575b-a5c0-09198c9d4fe7","op":"insert","key":"agent-analysis-backup-extension-ability-entry","previous_row_version":null,"row_version":1,"deleted":false},{"operation_id":"c710c49c-0ced-5606-8ea3-038d1e7a052b","op":"insert","key":"agent-analysis-distributed-abili